I am unpacking.
In a box there lies a picture.
It is a picture of my family.
My mother and my father are in the picture.
My sister Sofía and my brother Diego are there too.
And my dog, Lola.
They are all at home in Mexico.
I look at the picture for a long time.
There is a small shelf by my bed.
I pick up the picture.
I put it there.
Now the picture stands on the shelf by the bed.
I look at them again.
"Now you are here too," I say softly.
It is nice.
